{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These are "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"core"}]},{"type":"text","value":" options and API properties for all rows. More options and API properties are available for other "},{"type":"link","href":"../../guide/features.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"table features"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"row-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row API"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All row objects have the following properties:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"id","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"code","value":"id: string","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The resolved unique identifier for the row resolved via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.getRowId"},{"type":"text","value":" option. Defaults to the row's index (or relative index if it is a subRow)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"depth","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"depth"}]},{"type":"code","value":"depth: number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The depth of the row (if nested or grouped) relative to the root row array."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"index","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"index"}]},{"type":"code","value":"index: number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The index of the row within its parent array (or the root data array)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"original","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"original"}]},{"type":"code","value":"original: TData","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The original row object provided to the table."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🧠 If the row is a grouped row, the original row object will be the first original in the group."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parentid","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentId"}]},{"type":"code","value":"parentId?: string","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If nested, this row's parent row id."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getvalue","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getValue"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getValue: (columnId: string) => TValue","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the value from the row for a given columnId"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"rendervalue","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderValue"}]},{"type":"code","value":"renderValue: (columnId: string) => TValue","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renders the value from the row for a given columnId, but will return the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderFallbackValue"},{"type":"text","value":" if no value is found."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getuniquevalues","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getUniqueValues"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getUniqueValues: (columnId: string) => TValue[]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a unique array of values from the row for a given columnId."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"subrows","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subRows"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type subRows = Row<TData>[]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An array of subRows for the row as returned and created by the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.getSubRows"},{"type":"text","value":" option."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getparentrow","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getParentRow"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type getParentRow = () => Row<TData> | undefined","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the parent row for the row, if it exists."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getparentrows","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getParentRows"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type getParentRows = () => Row<TData>[]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the parent rows for the row, all the way up to a root row."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getleafrows","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getLeafRows"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type getLeafRows = () => Row<TData>[]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the leaf rows for the row, not including any parent rows."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"originalsubrows","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"originalSubRows"}]},{"type":"code","value":"originalSubRows?: TData[]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An array of the original subRows as returned by the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.getSubRows"},{"type":"text","value":" option."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getallcells","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAllCells"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type getAllCells = () => Cell<TData>[]","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns all of the "},{"type":"link","href":"./cell.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cells"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the row."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"row-api","text":"Row API","level":2},{"id":"id","text":"id","level":3},{"id":"depth","text":"depth","level":3},{"id":"index","text":"index","level":3},{"id":"original","text":"original","level":3},{"id":"parentid","text":"parentId","level":3},{"id":"getvalue","text":"getValue","level":3},{"id":"rendervalue","text":"renderValue","level":3},{"id":"getuniquevalues","text":"getUniqueValues","level":3},{"id":"subrows","text":"subRows","level":3},{"id":"getparentrow","text":"getParentRow","level":3},{"id":"getparentrows","text":"getParentRows","level":3},{"id":"getleafrows","text":"getLeafRows","level":3},{"id":"originalsubrows","text":"originalSubRows","level":3},{"id":"getallcells","text":"getAllCells","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThese are **core** options and API properties for all rows. More options and API properties are available for other [table features](../../guide/features.md).\n\n## Row API\n\nAll row objects have the following properties:\n\n### `id`\n\n```tsx\nid: string\n```\n\nThe resolved unique identifier for the row resolved via the `options.getRowId` option. Defaults to the row's index (or relative index if it is a subRow)\n\n### `depth`\n\n```tsx\ndepth: number\n```\n\nThe depth of the row (if nested or grouped) relative to the root row array.\n\n### `index`\n\n```tsx\nindex: number\n```\n\nThe index of the row within its parent array (or the root data array)\n\n### `original`\n\n```tsx\noriginal: TData\n```\n\nThe original row object provided to the table.\n\n> 🧠 If the row is a grouped row, the original row object will be the first original in the group.\n\n### `parentId`\n\n```tsx\nparentId?: string\n```\n\nIf nested, this row's parent row id.\n\n### `getValue`\n\n```tsx\ngetValue: (columnId: string) => TValue\n```\n\nReturns the value from the row for a given columnId\n\n### `renderValue`\n\n```tsx\nrenderValue: (columnId: string) => TValue\n```\n\nRenders the value from the row for a given columnId, but will return the `renderFallbackValue` if no value is found.\n\n### `getUniqueValues`\n\n```tsx\ngetUniqueValues: (columnId: string) => TValue[]\n```\n\nReturns a unique array of values from the row for a given columnId.\n\n### `subRows`\n\n```tsx\ntype subRows = Row<TData>[]\n```\n\nAn array of subRows for the row as returned and created by the `options.getSubRows` option.\n\n### `getParentRow`\n\n```tsx\ntype getParentRow = () => Row<TData> | undefined\n```\n\nReturns the parent row for the row, if it exists.\n\n### `getParentRows`\n\n```tsx\ntype getParentRows = () => Row<TData>[]\n```\n\nReturns the parent rows for the row, all the way up to a root row.\n\n### `getLeafRows`\n\n```tsx\ntype getLeafRows = () => Row<TData>[]\n```\n\nReturns the leaf rows for the row, not including any parent rows.\n\n### `originalSubRows`\n\n```tsx\noriginalSubRows?: TData[]\n```\n\nAn array of the original subRows as returned by the `options.getSubRows` option.\n\n### `getAllCells`\n\n```tsx\ntype getAllCells = () => Cell<TData>[]\n```\n\nReturns all of the [Cells](./cell.md) for the row.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Row APIs\n---\n\nThese are **core** options and API properties for all rows. More options and API properties are available for other [table features](../../guide/features.md).\n\n## Row API\n\nAll row objects have the following properties:\n\n### `id`\n\n```tsx\nid: string\n```\n\nThe resolved unique identifier for the row resolved via the `options.getRowId` option. Defaults to the row's index (or relative index if it is a subRow)\n\n### `depth`\n\n```tsx\ndepth: number\n```\n\nThe depth of the row (if nested or grouped) relative to the root row array.\n\n### `index`\n\n```tsx\nindex: number\n```\n\nThe index of the row within its parent array (or the root data array)\n\n### `original`\n\n```tsx\noriginal: TData\n```\n\nThe original row object provided to the table.\n\n> 🧠 If the row is a grouped row, the original row object will be the first original in the group.\n\n### `parentId`\n\n```tsx\nparentId?: string\n```\n\nIf nested, this row's parent row id.\n\n### `getValue`\n\n```tsx\ngetValue: (columnId: string) => TValue\n```\n\nReturns the value from the row for a given columnId\n\n### `renderValue`\n\n```tsx\nrenderValue: (columnId: string) => TValue\n```\n\nRenders the value from the row for a given columnId, but will return the `renderFallbackValue` if no value is found.\n\n### `getUniqueValues`\n\n```tsx\ngetUniqueValues: (columnId: string) => TValue[]\n```\n\nReturns a unique array of values from the row for a given columnId.\n\n### `subRows`\n\n```tsx\ntype subRows = Row<TData>[]\n```\n\nAn array of subRows for the row as returned and created by the `options.getSubRows` option.\n\n### `getParentRow`\n\n```tsx\ntype getParentRow = () => Row<TData> | undefined\n```\n\nReturns the parent row for the row, if it exists.\n\n### `getParentRows`\n\n```tsx\ntype getParentRows = () => Row<TData>[]\n```\n\nReturns the parent rows for the row, all the way up to a root row.\n\n### `getLeafRows`\n\n```tsx\ntype getLeafRows = () => Row<TData>[]\n```\n\nReturns the leaf rows for the row, not including any parent rows.\n\n### `originalSubRows`\n\n```tsx\noriginalSubRows?: TData[]\n```\n\nAn array of the original subRows as returned by the `options.getSubRows` option.\n\n### `getAllCells`\n\n```tsx\ntype getAllCells = () => Cell<TData>[]\n```\n\nReturns all of the [Cells](./cell.md) for the row.\n"}
